{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"async streams in c async streams in c","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md","fileName":"Async Streams in C#.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Async Streams in C#","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Files Streams and Serialization]] [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]] [[.NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Files Streams and Serialization",".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony",".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"async streams in c async streams in c","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md","fileName":"Async Streams in C#.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Async Streams in C#","heading":"Async Streams in C","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"C# 8 introduced asynchronous streams so a sequence can produce values over time without blocking while each value becomes available. A producer returns `IAsyncEnumerable<T>`, and a consumer processes it with `await foreach`.\n\nThis model combines the incremental nature of enumeration with asynchronous waiting, making it suitable for paged services, streamed data, and other sources that do not complete all at once. Cancellation and disposal remain important because enumeration may hold resources across multiple awaits.\n\nAn asynchronous stream returns `IAsyncEnumerable<T>` and is consumed with `await foreach`, allowing values to arrive incrementally through an asynchronous operation. This differs from awaiting one task that produces a single completed result.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Files Streams and Serialization",".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony",".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"async streams in c async streams in c","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Async Streams in C#.md","fileName":"Async Streams in C#.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Async Streams in C#","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n[[hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Files Streams and Serialization",".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony",".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}